-- The Schnorr oracle rows (S8b2, Q-S8b2-23 (a)). An scYes row says that
-- schnorrCheck accepts the signature of the C oracle (test/cryptotool.c,
-- sc_sign) by key 3 on the Fill message. An scNo row says that schnorrCheck
-- refuses a bad input: s + 1, m + 1, R off the curve, P off the curve, P at
-- infinity or s = r. A scTwin row says that the C builtin schnorrCheckC and
-- schnorrCheck give the same result on the Words of that row
-- (Q-S8b2-36 (a)). The Words of P and R are in Montgomery form, the Words of
-- s and m are canonical, and each Fe is 8 Words, least significant first.
-- One more scTwin row has R at the point at infinity (Q-S8b2-43 (a)):
-- ptOnCurve accepts (0, 0), and s = e k mod r for key 3 gives s G = e P.
-- No row has R = e P, the input for which the second ptMadd of scEquation
-- doubles a point. The challenge e is a hash of R, thus such an input
-- needs a value e that is equal to keccak256(e P, P, m) mod r (a fixed
-- point of the hash), and the oracle cannot calculate one.
-- These rows are not in test/crypto/crypto.lang: each heavy family of rows
-- has its own kit file (Q-S8b2-14 (a)). This is a kit file outside the Wasm
-- set. test/gate.sh evaluates each row with `langc --kit eval`.
def scYes : Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Word -> Nat :=
  fun (px0 : Word) (px1 : Word) (px2 : Word) (px3 : Word) (px4 : Word) (px5 : Word) (px6 : Word) (px7 : Word) (py0 : Word) (py1 : Word) (py2 : Word) (py3 : Word) (py4 : Word) (py5 : Word) (py6 : Word) (py7 : Word) (rx0 : Word) (rx1 : Word) (rx2 : Word) (rx3 : Word) (rx4 : Word) (rx5 : Word) (rx6 : Word) (rx7 : Word) (ry0 : Word) (ry1 : Word) (ry2 : Word) (ry3 : Word) (ry4 : Word) (ry5 : Word) (ry6 : Word) (ry7 : Word) (s0 : Word) (s1 : Word) (s2 : Word) (s3 : Word) (s4 : Word) (s5 : Word) (s6 : Word) (s7 : Word) (m0 : Word) (m1 : Word) (m2 : Word) (m3 : Word) (m4 : Word) (m5 : Word) (m6 : Word) (m7 : Word) =>
    either (fun (x : Unit) => 0) (fun (x : Unit) => 1) (schnorrCheck (pt1 (fe px0 px1 px2 px3 px4 px5 px6 px7) (fe py0 py1 py2 py3 py4 py5 py6 py7)) (pt1 (fe rx0 rx1 rx2 rx3 rx4 rx5 rx6 rx7) (fe ry0 ry1 ry2 ry3 ry4 ry5 ry6 ry7)) (fe s0 s1 s2 s3 s4 s5 s6 s7) (fe m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7))
